## Why This Is Asked
This question tests precise bit-manipulation skills across 128-bit data without loops or branches. It validates the ability to split work across halves and combine results safely while demonstrating understanding of efficient parallel counting algorithms.

## Key Concepts
- 128-bit values represented as two 64-bit halves
- SWAR (SIMD Within A Register) popcount on 64-bit words
- Combining two 64-bit counts to produce a 0-128 result
- Bitmask-based parallel computation

## Code Example
```c
uint64_t popcount64(uint64_t x) {
  x = x - ((x >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL);
  x = (x & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((x >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  x = (x + (x >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  x = x + (x >> 8);
  x = x + (x >> 16);
  x = x + (x >> 32);
  return x & 0x3FULL;
}

uint64_t popcount128(uint64_t hi, uint64_t lo) {
  return popcount64(hi) + popcount64(lo);
}
```

## Examples
- `popcount128(0x8000000000000000ULL, 0x0000000000000001ULL)` returns 2 (bits at positions 127 and 0)
- `popcount128(0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFULL, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFULL)` returns 128 (all bits set)

The SWAR algorithm processes all 64 bits in parallel using bitmasks to accumulate counts efficiently.

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to derive circular adjacency via rotation, and to implement a 128-bit popcount using SWAR style reductions; ensures understanding of cross-boundary bit relationships.

## Key Concepts

- Circular adjacency using ROTL
- 128-bit representation as two 64-bit halves
- SWAR/popcount with bitwise masks and shifts

## Code Example

```c
typedef struct { uint64_t hi; uint64_t lo; } uint128;

static inline uint128 rotl128(uint128 x){
  uint128 r;
  r.hi = (x.hi << 1) | (x.lo >> 63);
  r.lo = (x.lo << 1) | (x.hi >> 63);
  return r;
}

static inline unsigned int popcount128(uint128 x){
  uint64_t a = x.hi;
  uint64_t b = x.lo;
  a = a - ((a >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL);
  a = (a & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((a >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  a = (a + (a >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  unsigned int ca = (a * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;

  b = b - ((b >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL);
  b = (b & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((b >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  b = (b + (b >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  unsigned int cb = (b * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;

  return ca + cb;
}
```

